# Tor bridges — one bridge line per row, in the format published by
# https://bridges.torproject.org/.  Lines beginning with # and blank lines
# are ignored.  Example:
#
#   obfs4 1.2.3.4:443 FINGERPRINT cert=BASE64STUFF iat-mode=0
#
# Bridges are only used when the container detects at startup that direct
# connection to the Tor network is being filtered by your ISP.  On unfiltered
# networks this file is not consulted and bridges are not started.
#
# To obtain bridges:
#   - Web: https://bridges.torproject.org/
#   - Email: send "get transport obfs4" to bridges@torproject.org from a
#     Gmail or Riseup address.
#
# After adding bridges, restart the container:
#   docker compose restart
